## 📋 What Each File Does

### `app.py` (Main Application)
**Size**: ~8KB | **Lines**: ~250

The Streamlit web interface. Features:
- 🎭 6 story generation modes
- 🎙️ Real-time TTS narration
- 📥 Export to MP3/PDF
- 💾 Save & history
- ⚙️ Full customization controls

**To run:**
```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

### `src/qwen_engine.py` (Story Generation)
**Size**: ~4KB | **Lines**: ~150

Handles LLM story creation. Methods:
- `generate_story()` — Main story generation
- `generate_story_with_character()` — Character-focused tales
- `generate_mythology_remix()` — Modern folklore
- `refine_story()` — Edit existing stories

**Models:**
- Qwen 2.5 3B (7GB download)
- Auto-detects GPU/CPU

### `src/tts_engine.py` (Narration)
**Size**: ~5KB | **Lines**: ~180

Creates audio narration. Features:
- Piper TTS for natural voices
- Fallback to pyttsx3 if needed
- Multiple language support
- Speed adjustment (0.5x - 2.0x)

**Voices:**
- English (Indian)
- English (US)
- Hindi

### `src/config.py` (Configuration)
**Size**: ~3KB | **Lines**: ~120

Manages all settings:
- Model paths
- Output directories
- Defaults (temperature, tokens, etc.)
- System detection (GPU/CPU)
- Custom config loading

### `requirements.txt` (Dependencies)
**Size**: ~2KB

All Python packages needed:
- **Streamlit** — Web UI
- **Transformers** — HuggingFace models
- **Torch** — Deep learning (PyTorch)
- **Piper-TTS** — Text-to-speech
- **pyttsx3** — TTS fallback
- **Librosa** — Audio processing
- **ReportLab** — PDF generation
- And more...

### `install_dependencies.py` (Auto-Installer)
**Size**: ~8KB | **Lines**: ~250

Smart dependency installer that:
- ✅ Detects Python version
- ✅ Detects GPU/CPU
- ✅ Installs correct PyTorch
- ✅ Installs other packages
- ✅ Verifies installation

**Usage:**
```bash
python install_dependencies.py --gpu   # For NVIDIA GPU
python install_dependencies.py --cpu   # For CPU only
```

### `build_exe.py` (EXE Builder)
**Size**: ~6KB | **Lines**: ~200

Converts Streamlit app to Windows EXE:
- Creates standalone executable
- Bundles dependencies
- Output: ~500MB EXE file
- Uses PyInstaller

**Usage:**
